DATA SOURCE
===========

The RNA-seq data used in this project are not included in this repository
due to their size, and must be downloaded separately before running the
notebooks.

Source: Gene Expression Omnibus (GEO)
Series accession: GSE189053
Series page: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE189053

Direct download (all 40 samples, single .tar archive):
https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/download/?acc=GSE189053&format=file

Series title:
Transcriptome analysis of human DMD-K2957fs and CRISPR-corrected
(CORR-K2957fs) myogenic cultures during secondary myogenic differentiation.

Original publication:
Morera C, Kim J, Paredes-Redondo A, Nobles M, Rybin D, Kowala A, Meng J,
Liu P, Morgan JE, Muntoni F, Christoforou N, Owens J, Tinker A, Lin Y.
"CRISPR-mediated correction of skeletal muscle Ca2+ handling in a novel
DMD patient-derived pluripotent stem cell model."
Neuromuscul Disord. 2022 Dec;32(11-12):908-922. PMID: 36418198.

Contributed by: Pfizer Inc., Rare Disease Research Unit, Cambridge, MA, USA.

Overall design:
RNA sequencing was performed on DMD-K2957fs and CRISPR-corrected
(CORR-K2957fs) myogenic cultures during secondary differentiation at
5 time points (Day -1, 0, 2, 5 and 7). Four biological replicates were
performed per condition. 40 samples in total.

File format:
Each sample is provided as a compressed archive containing the raw
Salmon quantification output (transcript-level quant.sf file, not
gene-level counts). See 01_data_exploration.ipynb for the
transcript-to-gene aggregation step.

Instructions:
1. Download the .tar archive from the direct download link above
   (named GSE189053_RAW.tar).
2. Place it directly in this folder (data/raw/).
3. Run 01_data_exploration.ipynb, which extracts and processes the
   40 per-sample archives automatically.
